(b) Notwithstanding any other provision of this section, any person who was not qualified and registered to vote at the time of the adoption of this section shall not be required to re-register under the terms of this section unless that person shall have become or becomes disqualified to vote by reason of having been purged from the list of electors or for any other reason whatsoever, in which event those persons shall, in order to become registered to vote, re-register under the terms of this section.
